Run \href{https://github.com/USDA-ARS-GBRU/itsxpress}{ITSxpress} (Rivers et al.
2018; Einarsson & Rivers 2024) on paired-end or single-end FASTQ files to
trim off the conserved ribosomal flanks (SSU, 5.8S, LSU) while preserving
per-base Phred quality scores. Unlike \code{\link[=itsx_pq]{itsx_pq()}}, which runs ITSx on
already-denoised FASTA reference sequences in a \code{phyloseq} object,
\code{itsxpress_pq()} operates directly on raw FASTQ reads \strong{before} DADA2
denoising (\code{\link[=filter_trim]{filter_trim()}}, \code{\link[=denoised_reads]{denoised_reads()}}).

By default (\code{paired_end = TRUE} and \code{single_file_output = FALSE}),
\code{itsxpress_pq()} writes unmerged forward and reverse trimmed FASTQ files
(\code{--outfile} and \code{--outfile2}), which is the layout required for DADA2's
paired-end error model.
}
